{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"OPERATOR DECISION (AC1): accepted, via operator-approved task dispatched to this session — implement the provenance marker as proposed. Design adjudication: the marker is an OPTIONAL 'provenance' field on the caused_by LINK event payload with values 'derived' (blame auto-derivation) | 'explicit' (operator/agent-supplied), rather than the sketched 'derived: blame|explicit' spelling — a field named 'derived' holding value 'explicit' is self-contradictory on read. Old events carry no field and read as unknown. No change to the deriver's fail-closed behaviour. Builds on merged change 2125 (77e7-1eec-7b52-46ed, caused_by target validation) — branched from its merge commit d432e3c49b6."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787442972884044001,"uuid":"3291d2ca-9e72-4cae-b2e7-695aa414f9e2"}